Features of Global Enterprises
Foreign Collaboration: Global enterprises usually collaborate
with Indian companies (public or private) for production of
goods, use of brand names or for sale of technology.
They have to comply with various restrictive clauses for
agreements relating to transfer of technology, pricing,
dividend payments, etc.
Big industrial houses collaborate with MNCs in order to
diversify and expand in terms of patents, resources, foreign
exchange, etc.
